course: dictionary
lesson: 1086
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: The word brace has several meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one is meant. Start with the clues: what is happening, and who or what is involved?
explain: Ellie has braces on her teeth, so braces must be the metal or plastic device that straightens teeth. If the sentence was about trousers, you would know braces meant straps. Always check the clues before you choose a meaning.
explain: «Brace yourself» is a phrase that warns you something difficult is coming. If you read «brace yourself for a bumpy landing», you know it means get ready. Then test your meaning in the sentence: does it still make sense? If it does, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: The same word can have several meanings, and context tells you which one is right.
fact: «Brace» can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action), and its meaning changes with its job in the sentence.
fact: «Brace yourself» means get ready for something difficult or a hit.
fact: A «knee brace» is a support that holds a hurt or weak knee steady.
fact: «Braces» in maths and computing are curly brackets { }, which group things together.
exercise: Ellie has braces on her teeth to straighten them. What are braces here? | *A metal or plastic device fixed to teeth | A curly bracket used in maths | A support for a broken knee | Straps that hold up trousers
exercise: Brace yourself for a bumpy landing. What does brace yourself mean? | *Get ready for something difficult | Shout for help | Buy a new coat | Fall fast asleep
exercise: «Use the brace { } to group the numbers in your sum.» What is a curly bracket like this called in maths? | Hook | *Brace | Arrow | Tail
test: «He had to brace the ladder with his foot so it would not slip.» What does brace mean here? | Paint | Wash | Run fast | *To press firmly so it stays steady
test: A knee brace helps a hurt knee stay still while it heals. What does a brace do? | *It holds a weak body part steady | It is a bandage for a cut | It warms the knee up | It makes the knee bend more
exam: Ben's dad wears braces to hold up his trousers. In America, what would people call them? | Scarves | *Suspenders | Belts | Ropes
